WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.179
Battery performance changes with temperature.

00:00:02.179 --> 00:00:07.169
In cold conditions, chemical reactions slow and voltage may sag under load,

00:00:07.169 --> 00:00:09.249
reducing usable energy and power.

00:00:09.249 --> 00:00:14.655
A battery that appears charged can reach a critical state sooner than expected.

00:00:14.655 --> 00:00:17.982
Follow approved guidance for battery temperature and preconditioning.

00:00:17.982 --> 00:00:21.308
Keep batteries in a suitable environment before use,

00:00:21.308 --> 00:00:26.298
confirm they have reached an acceptable operating condition, and avoid improvised heating.

00:00:26.298 --> 00:00:30.041
Plan shorter flights and larger reserves in the cold.

00:00:30.041 --> 00:00:31.705
Heat creates different risks.

00:00:31.705 --> 00:00:35.031
High ambient temperature, direct sun, heavy processing, hovering,

00:00:35.031 --> 00:00:40.022
and repeated flights can stress batteries, motors, electronics, mobile devices, and payloads.

00:00:40.022 --> 00:00:44.596
Overheated components may throttle, shut down, age faster, or behave unpredictably.

00:00:44.596 --> 00:00:47.091
Monitor more than a percentage display.

00:00:47.091 --> 00:00:52.497
Observe voltage or cell status when available, temperature warnings, power demand, battery age,

00:00:52.497 --> 00:00:57.071
prior damage, swelling, and the difference between planned and actual consumption.

00:00:57.071 --> 00:01:00.398
Treat unexpected behavior as a reason to recover.

00:01:00.398 --> 00:01:02.477
Storage and transport affect safety.

00:01:02.477 --> 00:01:06.636
Protect batteries from physical damage, moisture, extreme temperature, conductive objects,

00:01:06.636 --> 00:01:08.299
and unattended hot vehicles.

00:01:08.299 --> 00:01:11.210
Use approved charging, storage, and retirement practices,

00:01:11.210 --> 00:01:14.537
and isolate questionable batteries according to organizational procedures.

00:01:14.537 --> 00:01:17.032
Temperature also affects people and data.

00:01:17.032 --> 00:01:22.438
Cold hands, heat stress, screen dimming, condensation, and sensor drift can degrade decisions.

00:01:22.438 --> 00:01:28.260
Environmental planning includes crew endurance and payload quality as well as aircraft flight time.
